{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546169731,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb7c666ffeHkmmUEjhPLtmeU","part":{"partID":"prt_1d34976ac001W2H5ajnu0nlLt1","sessionID":"ses_e2cb7c666ffeHkmmUEjhPLtmeU","messageID":"msg_1d3495a69001PlM1nXPkBuQ4cr","type":"tool","id":"call_429931d0278e4dc7921146f1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: description: \"List every doctor target and run the read-only setup checks, naming the repair command for each failing leg.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob\n5: ---\n6: <!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n7: \n8: # /doctor:setup Router\n9: \n10: This command is a thin, read-only router. It lists every doctor command and target with what each checks, runs the existing read-only checks once, and prints the runnable repair command for each failing leg. It writes nothing in the repository.\n11: \n12: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n13: \n14: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n15: \n16: Load the presentation contract before showing any dashboard, result summary, or next-step text.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n25: | Workflow | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n26: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest. This command owns the route whose `command` is `/doctor:setup`.\n33: - `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`.\n34: - The command takes no positional target and no flag, so `/doctor:setup` alone runs it.\n35: - Any positional or flag fails before YAML load with the presentation contract's argument error.\n36: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n37: - The YAML owns workflow behavior. The presentation Markdown owns visible wording and layout.\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n42: \n43: | Target | Workflow |\n44: |--------|----------|\n45: | `setup` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n46: \n47: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n48: 2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and select the `/doctor:setup` route.\n49: 3. Load `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` and execute it step by step.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n54: \n55: The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates and next-step text live only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs six read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors.\n63: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n64: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n65: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n66: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n67: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n68: It shows an open-notes line while any handoff note is still unclaimed.\n69: It shows the Claude context window the relaunch nudge measures against, or the two settings that supply one when none is configured.\n70: It shows an orphans line from `orphan-process-check.cjs --summary`.\n71: That line counts leftover helper processes and model servers whose launcher died.\n72: These lines are informational and never change the status.\n73: It writes nothing in the repository and never starts the advisor daemon.\n74: The only write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory when that directory is absent.\n75: The default socket directory is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`.\n76: The advisor leg reports PASS when exit 0 has `data.freshness` set to `live`.\n77: It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n78: It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n79: It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n80: It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: description: \"List every doctor target and run the read-only setup checks, naming the repair command for each failing leg.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob\n5: ---\n6: <!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n7: \n8: # /doctor:setup Router\n9: \n10: This command is a thin, read-only router. It lists every doctor command and target with what each checks, runs the existing read-only checks once, and prints the runnable repair command for each failing leg. It writes nothing in the repository.\n11: \n12: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n13: \n14: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n15: \n16: Load the presentation contract before showing any dashboard, result summary, or next-step text.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n25: | Workflow | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n26: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest. This command owns the route whose `command` is `/doctor:setup`.\n33: - `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`.\n34: - The command takes no positional target and no flag, so `/doctor:setup` alone runs it.\n35: - Any positional or flag fails before YAML load with the presentation contract's argument error.\n36: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n37: - The YAML owns workflow behavior. The presentation Markdown owns visible wording and layout.\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n42: \n43: | Target | Workflow |\n44: |--------|----------|\n45: | `setup` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n46: \n47: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n48: 2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and select the `/doctor:setup` route.\n49: 3. Load `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` and execute it step by step.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n54: \n55: The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates and next-step text live only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs six read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors.\n63: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n64: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n65: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n66: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n67: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n68: It shows an open-notes line while any handoff note is still unclaimed.\n69: It shows the Claude context window the relaunch nudge measures against, or the two settings that supply one when none is configured.\n70: It shows an orphans line from `orphan-process-check.cjs --summary`.\n71: That line counts leftover helper processes and model servers whose launcher died.\n72: These lines are informational and never change the status.\n73: It writes nothing in the repository and never starts the advisor daemon.\n74: The only write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory when that directory is absent.\n75: The default socket directory is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`.\n76: The advisor leg reports PASS when exit 0 has `data.freshness` set to `live`.\n77: It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n78: It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n79: It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n80: It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794546169516,"end":1794546169731}}}}
