{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546200083,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb7c666ffeHkmmUEjhPLtmeU","part":{"partID":"prt_1d349ec71001QUz9AY2uRg50f3","sessionID":"ses_e2cb7c666ffeHkmmUEjhPLtmeU","messageID":"msg_1d349e028001JpSwaRl5CBwP5d","type":"tool","id":"call_a1d2b4c91c004b9ca889b1d5","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"offset":59,"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md","limit":10},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 59-68\n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n63: The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n64: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n65: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n66: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n67: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n68: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 69]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 59-68\n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n63: The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n64: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n65: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n66: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n67: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n68: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 69]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"offset\":59,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\",\"limit\":10}"},"time":{"start":1794546199665,"end":1794546200083}}}}
